# RS_ShieldSaw -- the mark a blocked blow leaves on the plate.
#
# A ONE-UNIT QUAD AND NOTHING ELSE. Two triangles, four vertices, one UV square. It is
# authored as OBJ rather than MD3 because this engine loads both and OBJ is text: a quad this
# small written as binary MD3 is a file nobody can check by reading it, and the one property
# that matters here -- which way it faces -- would be invisible.
#
# AXES. The quad lies in the X/Y plane with its normal along +Z in OBJ space. The shield's
# front plate faces mesh -Y, so the MODELDEF block that uses this rotates it onto the plate;
# keeping the mesh itself axis-aligned means the rotation is stated in one place and can be
# read, instead of being baked into vertex numbers.
#
# SIZE. One unit across, centred on the origin, so the MODELDEF Scale IS the dent's diameter
# in mesh units and a caller choosing a size is choosing a number with a meaning.

# no mtllib: this engine takes the skin from MODELDEF, and the OBJ loader has no mtllib
# handling at all -- naming a material file that does not exist is a warning waiting to happen.
o dent

v -0.5 -0.5 0.0
v  0.5 -0.5 0.0
v  0.5  0.5 0.0
v -0.5  0.5 0.0

vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 1.0 1.0
vt 0.0 1.0

vn 0.0 0.0 1.0

# The material name must RESOLVE: the loader calls LoadSkin on it, first by bare name and
# then relative to this file, so it has to be the texture sitting next to this model. A made-up
# group name fails the model load outright ("Material dentskin (#0) not found").
usemtl dent_scorch
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1
f 1/1/1 3/3/1 4/4/1
